  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "David bought $1$ foot of decorative ribbon and paid $$1.20$ for it. What's the unit price per yard?\n\nAssume that there are $3$ feet in one yard.",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that there are $3$ feet in each yard.  \n\nSince the price is $$1.20$ per foot, to find the price per yard, we multiply by $3:$\n\n$$\n1.20\\times 3=3.60\n$$\n\nTherefore, the decorative ribbon costs $$3.60$ per yard.",
